    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent storage duration for DNA samples",
      "page": 113,
      "quote": "Samples will be stored for a maximum of 15 years from the date of last patient last visit, after which they will be destroyed.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Typographical error: 'withdrawal' instead of 'withdraw'",
      "page": 114,
      "quote": "the patient understands that they may freely withdrawal from the genetic aspect of the study at any time.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Typographical error: 'during for'",
      "page": 110,
      "quote": "will be tracked by the appropriate AstraZeneca Team during for the remainder of the sample life cycle.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent definition of Hy's Law: PHL definition uses '>' for TBL, HL definition uses '>' but text says '> 2 x ULN' consistently; no issue",
